        <h2 id="why-wrists">Why Wrist Strength Matters for Dead Hangs</h2>
        <p>Your wrist is the bridge between your forearm muscles and your fingers. Force from the forearm flexors passes through the wrist joint on its way to the bar. Wrist comfort affects how long you can hang.</p>
        <p>The wrist joint contains 8 carpal bones, multiple ligaments and the tendons of the muscles that control your hand. The joint has little bony constraint. The wrist muscles contribute to its stability.</p>
        <p>Wrist problems that people report with dead hang training include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Wrist pain during hanging:</strong> It has several possible causes, including grip position, rapid volume increases and injury. See a clinician if it persists.</li>
          <li><strong>Tendonitis at the wrist:</strong> It can follow rapid training volume increases without enough preparation.</li>
          <li><strong>Tingling or numbness in the hand:</strong> It can come from carpal tunnel syndrome and other causes.</li>
          <li><strong>Ulnar-side wrist pain:</strong> Pain on the pinky side can come from several structures. See a clinician for diagnosis.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The exercises below cover mobility, strengthening and rehabilitation work. They do not diagnose or treat any of these problems. See a clinician for a diagnosis.</p>

        <h2 id="warmup">Warm-Up Exercises (Do These Daily)</h2>
        <p>Many people do these mobility exercises before a dead hang session and as a daily habit during desk work. Total time: 3 to 5 minutes. The sets, reps and frequencies on this page are common training practice, not a tested prescription.</p>

        <h3>1. Wrist Circles</h3>
        <p>Interlace your fingers and rotate your wrists in slow circles. Perform 15 rotations clockwise then 15 counterclockwise. Move through the full range of motion, including flexion, extension, ulnar deviation and radial deviation, in one smooth circle.</p>
        <p class="table-cue">Scroll the table horizontally on smaller screens.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable comparison table" tabindex="0"><table class="data-table">
