          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Gentle loading during injury recovery</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Hold</td><td>10 sec × 4 directions × 3 rounds</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Intensity</td><td>Light effort, pain free</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Progression</td><td>Increase hold time first, then force, only while pain free</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <h3>12. Eccentric Wrist Curls (Rehab Protocol)</h3>
        <p>Perform only the lowering phase of a wrist curl. Use your other hand to lift the weight into the curled position, then slowly lower with the working wrist over 5 seconds. Eccentric loading is commonly used for tendinopathy. The evidence for wrist tendons is limited.</p>
