        <h2 id="routine">Complete Wrist Routine</h2>
        <p>This wrist routine covers warm-up, strengthening and maintenance in a single 15-minute session. Perform it before dead hang training or as a standalone wrist session.</p>

        <p class="table-cue">Scroll the table horizontally on smaller screens.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable comparison table" tabindex="0"><table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Phase</th>
              <th scope="col">Exercise</th>
              <th scope="col">Sets × Reps</th>
              <th scope="col">Time</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td rowspan="4"><strong>Warm-Up</strong></td><td>Wrist Circles</td><td>15 each direction</td><td rowspan="4">3 min</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Prayer Stretch</td><td>2 × 20 sec</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reverse Prayer Stretch</td><td>2 × 20 sec</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tabletop Wrist Rocks</td><td>10 each direction</td></tr>
            <tr><td rowspan="4"><strong>Strengthen</strong></td><td>Wrist Curls</td><td>3 × 15</td><td rowspan="4">10 min</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reverse Wrist Curls</td><td>3 × 15</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Radial/Ulnar Deviation</td><td>2 × 12 each</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rubber Band Extensions</td><td>3 × 20</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Cool-Down</strong></td><td>Prayer + Reverse Prayer</td><td>30 sec each</td><td>2 min</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Before dead hangs:</strong> Do the warm-up phase only (3 minutes). Save the strengthening phase for after your dead hang session or a separate time. Fatigued wrist muscles can cut your hang time.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="programming">Programming Guidelines</h2>

        <h3>Frequency</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mobility exercises (warm-up phase):</strong> Many people do them daily, 3 to 5 minutes before training and during desk work breaks.</li>
          <li><strong>Strengthening exercises:</strong> 3 to 4 times per week, with at least one rest day between sessions.</li>
          <li><strong>Rehab exercises:</strong> Often done daily while managing pain or recovering from injury, as a clinician advises. Reduce to 3 times weekly once symptoms resolve.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Progression</h3>
        <p>Wrist muscles are small, so progress slowly:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A common approach is to raise the weight by about 1 lb every 2 weeks, which is slower than for large muscle groups</li>
          <li>Add 2 to 3 reps per set before increasing weight</li>
          <li>Do not train wrist exercises to absolute failure; stop 1 to 2 reps short</li>
          <li>If you feel sharp pain during any exercise, stop and lower the weight</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Integration With Dead Hang Training</h3>
        <p>Wrist exercises can complement dead hangs by working muscles that dead hangs alone do not target. Dead hangs load the grip muscles isometrically but do not train wrist extension, radial and ulnar deviation or forearm rotation.</p>
